<p>Checked on 20 October 2026. Native observations use PostgreSQL 18.6 (Homebrew), Node.js 24.16.0, pg 8.23.1 and OpenSSL 4.0.3 on one Apple-silicon laptop. The downloadable fixture uses dummy local data and self-created CAs; it establishes selected connection and authority paths, not production or managed-service security. All five figures are illustrative.</p>
